x86_64-windows  a virtual base is laid out by a vbtable on this ABI, not by a vbase_offset in the vftable, and none of it has been measured against cl. Measured on the Windows box: cl gives `struct D1 : virtual V` sizeof 24 with V at +16 and D1's own member at +8, where cxx1 gives 16 - so the layout this target already emits disagrees with its own oracle, and reading a member of a virtual base stops with `codegen: this has no address`. cxx1 refuses this case today for a different and now-inaccurate reason - the multiple-inheritance guard in ParserClass.cpp fires because hasVptr() became `polymorphic() || hasVirtualBase()`, so it reports "virtual functions in a base that is not the first" for a class with no virtual functions at all. Both wants a named refusal for virtual bases on this target. What this case measures - that a virtual base is constructed once, by the most-derived class - is an Itanium question until that lands.
